'''Anderson França Varejão''' ({{IPAc-en|ˌ|v|ɑː|r|ə|ˈ|ʒ|aʊ|n}} {{respell|VAH|rə|ZHOWN}}; {{IPA|pt|ˈɐ̃deʁsõ ˈfɾɐ̃sɐ vɐɾeˈʒɐ̃w}}; born September 28, 1982) is a Brazilian former professional [[basketball]] player who is currently a Player Development Consultant and Global Ambassador for the [[Cleveland Cavaliers]], where he spent 13 of his 14 seasons in the [[National Basketball Association]] (NBA). With a career that spanned four professional leagues, Varejão also played for [[Franca Basquetebol Clube|Franca]] and the [[Flamengo Basketball|Flamengo]] of the [[Novo Basquete Brasil]] (NBB), [[FC Barcelona Bàsquet|Barcelona]] of the [[EuroLeague]] and [[Liga ACB]], and has been a regular member of the [[Brazil national basketball team|Brazilian national team]], winning a gold medal in 2003 at the [[Basketball at the 2003 Pan American Games|Pan American Games]].

